From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:18:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Take over: pin an EPERM writer to the ACK deadline;
 a failed reset save keeps the 4090 refusal

Follow-up to #1252 review (t_01a1ce87ed6dd1df). The foreign-pid-namespace
test is owned by #1531.

- test: a same-namespace pid whose kill(pid, 0) answers EPERM is not provably
  alive, so Take over is refused 4090 SESSION_NOT_OWNED at the ACK deadline,
  not after the live-writer cap. Coverage of existing behaviour; it kills the
  mutant that treats PermissionError as alive.
- Desktop sendIdentityless: if saving legacyAttempted=false after a definite
  refusal rejects, warn '[prepared-submission-reset]' and rethrow the original
  refusal instead of the storage error.
